# Initial Sketches (Conceptual Wireframes)

## 1. Mobile Home Screen

* Large central temperature display (e.g., 22°C)
* Circular dial or slider for adjusting temperature
* Current status:

  * “Heating…” / “Cooling…” / “Idle”
* Quick buttons:

  * Heat
  * Cool
  * Schedule
* Bottom navigation:

  * Home | Schedule | Settings

---

## 2. Schedule Screen

* Weekly calendar view (tabs: Weekdays / Weekend)
* Timeline sliders:

  * Morning / Day / Evening / Night
* Toggle:

  * “Auto-detect weekends”
* Add/Edit schedule button

---

## 3. Settings Screen

* Temperature units (°C / °F)
* Offline mode indicator:

  * “Connected locally” / “No internet – local control active”
* Device pairing / network settings
* Energy-saving mode toggle

---

## 4. Desktop View (Responsive Layout)

* Split layout:

  * Left: temperature dial
  * Right: schedule overview
* Top bar:

  * Device status
  * User profile
* More detailed analytics (optional):

  * Energy usage graph

---

## 5. Offline Mode UI State

* Banner at top:

  * “Offline mode: Connected via local network”
* Disable cloud-only features
* Keep temperature + scheduling active

---

# User Stories

### Core Control

* As a homeowner, I want to adjust the temperature remotely, so that my home is comfortable when I arrive.
* As a user, I want to quickly increase or decrease temperature, so that I can react instantly to weather changes.

### Scheduling

* As a busy professional, I want to set weekday and weekend schedules, so that my home adapts to my routine automatically.
* As a user, I want the system to detect weekends automatically, so that I don’t need to manually switch schedules.

### Offline Capability

* As a user, I want to control my thermostat without internet, so that I am not dependent on cloud services.
* As a user, I want to see connection status, so that I understand system limitations.

### Multi-Device Use

* As a user, I want to access the app from any device/browser, so that I am not restricted to one platform.

### Energy Efficiency

* As an eco-conscious user, I want to automatically lower temperature at night, so that I save energy and reduce costs.

---

#  Use Cases

---

## Use Case 1: Adjust Temperature Remotely

Actor: User (Alex)
Precondition: User is connected to the thermostat (internet or local network)

Main Flow:

1. User opens the web app on their phone
2. System displays current temperature
3. User adjusts temperature to 22°C
4. System sends command to thermostat
5. Thermostat begins heating

System Response:

* Updates UI to show “Heating to 22°C”
* Confirms change visually (animation or highlight)

---

## Use Case 2: Set Weekly Schedule

Actor: User (Priya)
Precondition: Schedule feature is available

Main Flow:

1. User navigates to Schedule screen
2. User selects “Weekdays”
3. Sets temperature drop at 10 PM
4. Switches to “Weekend”
5. Sets temperature drop at 12 AM
6. Saves schedule

System Response:

* Stores schedule locally and/or in cloud
* Displays confirmation message
* Applies schedule automatically based on day detection

---

## Use Case 3: Offline Control

Actor: User
Precondition: Internet is down, local network available

Main Flow:

1. User opens web app
2. System detects no internet
3. Connects via local network
4. User adjusts temperature

System Response:

* Displays “Offline Mode Active”
* Executes command locally
* Maintains full control functionality

---

## Use Case 4: Automatic Weekend Detection

Actor: System

Main Flow:

1. System checks current day
2. Identifies weekday vs weekend
3. Loads appropriate schedule

System Response:

* Applies correct temperature settings
* Updates UI to reflect active schedule

---

#  Optional Enhancements (Nice-to-have)

* Smart suggestions (e.g., “Lower temp to save energy tonight?”)
* Geofencing (auto-adjust when user is near home)
* Voice control integration
* Energy usage insights dashboard

